    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5cb3ca3_81d11a9e",
        "filename": "drivers/android/binder.c",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 2922,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-26T22:58:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the point of tmp_refs is to prevent weak from going to 0 prematurely -- it needs to keep the node alive. So the user doesn\u0027t need to be notified if tmp_refs is inc/dec, but user space must not be told that all references are gone if tmp_refs !\u003d 0.",
      "parentUuid": "07e72345_809dbfdd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2922,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 2922,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "37bfde2c176d875f08eebf137f99773300c1c3ea",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ebc57ad9_c662701f",
        "filename": "drivers/android/binder.c",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 2922,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-26T23:04:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think that is strictly true. If tmp_refs is the only reference to a node, user-space must also have a local reference to the node before another reference can be added in the driver.",
      "parentUuid": "c5cb3ca3_81d11a9e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2922,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 2922,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "37bfde2c176d875f08eebf137f99773300c1c3ea",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7fbf0316_10ab91d7",
        "filename": "drivers/android/binder.c",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 2922,
